    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d470">

                <pb facs="0531" n="427" xml:id="pg427"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.00 Revolutions/413: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at São Paulo</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cameron</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">São Paulo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-10-13T10:00:00-02:00">October 13,
                            1932—10 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 13—7:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Yesterday afternoon mob broke windows various stores whose proprietors considered
                    unfriendly to São Paulo. Eight killed; considerable number wounded by police
                    during rioting. All São Paulo leaders recommending peaceful attitude. No serious
                    disorders expected.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Embassy at Rio de Janeiro.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cameron</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
